cam/
└── cam.py   — MicroPython camera firmware (runs on OpenMV H7 Plus)
                Detects blue goal, yellow goal, and orange ball via colour blobs.
                Outputs a CSV line over UART every frame:

                  BX,<x>,<y>,<dist>,<angle>,<lb_dist>,<lb_angle>,
                  BY,<x>,<y>,<dist>,<angle>,<lb_dist>,<lb_angle>,
                  BALL,<x>,<y>,<dist>,<angle>

                Layer 2 reads this on Serial3 via cam_comm.

Key tuning constants (top of cam.py):
  window_x / window_y     — capture resolution (default 480×480)
  OPTICAL_OFFSET_X/Y      — lens centre correction
  BALL_ROI_SIZE           — square ROI for ball detection
  DEBUG_* flags           — enable/disable drawing overlays and serial debug prints

Coordinate convention:
  x/y — pixel coordinates, origin top-left
  dist — approximate distance derived from blob area (arbitrary units)
  angle — angle to blob centre relative to image centre, degrees
  lb_* — largest-blob variant used for scoring aim
